(5455783, 781872, 102315, '<td valign="top">If you don''t mind me asking. How did you get this image so sharp. Is it all in the lens? Does it have a lot to do with PP? I have been trying to get a B&amp;W to look good and can come no where near this. Please PM me if you get a moment.</td>', 'If you don''t mind me asking. How did you get this image so sharp. Is it all in the lens? Does it have a lot to do with PP? I have been trying to get a B&W to look good and can come no where near this. Please PM me if you get a moment.', '2009-04-28 16:15:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5455820, 783541, 62787, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! :) (again - it seems to like me pulling out your images)<br/> <br/>Good capture - as you say, the body language works perfectly. And an interesting, personal take on the challenge - I can certainly identify with that nightmare. <br/> <br/>In this case, I think the original capture is good, but that different post-processing could have been used to convey the message more effectively.  I don''t normally like selective desats, and I do think here it works rather well, though I wonder if a more gradual, softened selective desat would have worked better (so, like, fading out the colour more and more as you move away from the girl). Also, the background seems to contravene the message of the shot, since there are these pretty white flowers, a big white tent etc. I''d be tempted to make liberal use of dodging/burning/vignetting/overlays/soft light layers to add a more contrasty/edgy/nightmarish feel to the surroundings. Also watch out for signs of oversharpening - it might have been intentional, but I find the sharpening halos quite distracting, there are other ways of increasing contrast that don''t produce the same artefacts.<br/> <br/>Anyway, as I said, I think it''s a cool shot, but I''d like to see you spend some quality time in Photoshop with it, have a few more shots and see what you can do with it. (do post any interesting experimental results :) )</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! :) (again - it seems to like me pulling out your images) Good capture - as you say, the body language works perfectly. And an interesting, personal take on the challenge - I can certainly identify with that nightmare.  In this case, I think the original capture is good, but that different post-processing could have been used to convey the message more effectively.  I don''t normally like selective desats, and I do think here it works rather well, though I wonder if a more gradual, softened selective desat would have worked better (so, like, fading out the colour more and more as you move away from the girl). Also, the background seems to contravene the message of the shot, since there are these pretty white flowers, a big white tent etc. I''d be tempted to make liberal use of dodging/burning/vignetting/overlays/soft light layers to add a more contrasty/edgy/nightmarish feel to the surroundings. Also watch out for signs of oversharpening - it might have been intentional, but I find the sharpening halos quite distracting, there are other ways of increasing contrast that don''t produce the same artefacts. Anyway, as I said, I think it''s a cool shot, but I''d like to see you spend some quality time in Photoshop with it, have a few more shots and see what you can do with it. (do post any interesting experimental results :) )', '2009-04-28 16:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5456197, 783765, 66384, '<td valign="top">I was at the dentist yesterday, and noticed he looked very much like this. I showed him the photo on my iPhone, and he thought it was a hoot. He especially liked the eyes -- me too -- but he was also very interested in the details of the equipment. You did a great job on this. Can''t imagine how you managed it alone.</td>', 'I was at the dentist yesterday, and noticed he looked very much like this. I showed him the photo on my iPhone, and he thought it was a hoot. He especially liked the eyes -- me too -- but he was also very interested in the details of the equipment. You did a great job on this. Can''t imagine how you managed it alone.', '2009-04-28 23:21:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5456223, 781872, 47470, '<td valign="top">I''ve taken showers with frogs (and geckos and bugs and other strange creatures...no snakes though I think) more times than I can count.  It''s just what happens when you camp in Africa : )  But I do remember my fellow travelers being incredibly creeped out.  I wonder if any of them had nightmares about it later?<br/> <br/>Anyway, cool shot!  Congrats on the top 15!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-28 22:46:25.</i></td>', 'I''ve taken showers with frogs (and geckos and bugs and other strange creatures...no snakes though I think) more times than I can count.  It''s just what happens when you camp in Africa : )  But I do remember my fellow travelers being incredibly creeped out.  I wonder if any of them had nightmares about it later? Anyway, cool shot!  Congrats on the top 15!', '2009-04-28 23:44:48.000000', '2009-04-28 23:46:25.000000', 0),
